name: Review keeps its page and historical source when a generation is replaced
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finding_continuity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 rows 1-500 of 800 | first-page
nav-mode:
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 25 501-800/800 | later-page
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
require-live-snap: 15 open F- | open-draft
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: confirmed | opened-source
expect: DECISION SOURCE
expect-echo-within: 300 retained-continuity-draft
live-snap: retained-draft
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finding_continuity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART replace
require-live-snap: 25 pinned outside list | historical-source-retained
expect: 501-800/800
expect: retained-continuity-draft
expect-not: Selected finding left this query
ask: Does the new observation keep the later ledger page and composer draft while clearly retaining the historical pin instead of silently changing its source?
keys: C-u
nav-mode:
keys: q
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 continuity-later | latest-source-opened
submit: decision deferred J145 current observation deliberately deferred
nav-mode:
keys: g
require-live-snap: 25 J145 current observation deliberately deferred | current-source-decision
expect: 501-800/800
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finding_continuity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART decided
ask: Does explicitly opening the current row make the new decision refer to the new observation, with the earlier decision preserved?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: continuity-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: continuity-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: continuity-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: continuity-60x20
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | narrow-detail-opened
resize: 40x12
live-snap: continuity-40x12
expect: F-0601
expect: 300/800 findings loaded
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-1
expect: DECISION
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-2
expect: recorded: deferred
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-3
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-4
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 501-800/800 | tiny-list-restored
ask: Can the operator inspect the same finding and its page at all six sizes through the visible controls, without more discovery work?
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 rows 1-500 of 800 | recovered-first
nav-mode:
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 25 501-800/800 | recovered-later
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
require-live-snap: 15 open F- | recovered-open-draft
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 J145 current observation deliberately deferred | recovered-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finding_continuity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does no-color restart recover both observations and decisions with stable page access, no provider requests and no further source changes?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
